From: SlicerWeb <slicerweb@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] BUG: Do not draw wide lines with a geometry shader in GLES builds

Lines wider than the widest the hardware draws are drawn by VTK with a geometry
shader, which a build for OpenGL ES (WebAssembly, WebGL) has not got: vtkShader
refuses it ("Geometry shaders are not supported in this build of VTK"), the shader
program is never set, and nothing of that actor is drawn - not even thin lines.
In 3D Slicer this took the interaction handles of markups (drawn by
vtkOpenGLGlyph3DHelper) and the outlines of widgets with it.

Where there is no geometry shader the wide line path cannot work, so it is not
taken and the lines are drawn plain, one pixel wide.
---
diff --git a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper.cxx b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper.cxx
index c015595..a18f9bc 100644
--- a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper.cxx
@@ -368,6 +368,14 @@ void vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper::BuildShaders(
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 bool vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper::HaveWideLines(vtkRenderer* ren, vtkActor* actor)
 {
+#ifndef GL_GEOMETRY_SHADER
+  // Lines wider than one pixel are drawn with a geometry shader, which this build has not got
+  // (OpenGL ES): asking for one leaves the shader program unset and nothing of the actor drawn, so
+  // plain lines are drawn instead.
+  (void)ren;
+  (void)actor;
+  return false;
+#else
   vtkHardwareSelector* selector = ren->GetSelector();
   if (selector && selector->GetFieldAssociation() == vtkDataObject::FIELD_ASSOCIATION_POINTS)
   {
@@ -387,6 +395,7 @@ bool vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper::HaveWideLines(vtkRenderer* ren, vtkActor* actor)
   }
   return this->DrawingSelection &&
     (this->GetOpenGLMode(this->SelectionType, this->LastBoundBO->PrimitiveType) == GL_LINES);
+#endif
 }
 
